{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>He who watches</b>. This too is a parable about the generous man, for the lazy, miserly sower will say: This wind portends that no rain will fall in the coming days — so why should I take what I have, namely the seed, and bury it in the earth? And some say it is a commandment according to its plain meaning for the sower, since Solomon has already mentioned that there is no craft like the working of the land; therefore one must not rely on his own knowledge and on everything he has tested, for the times change."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:07.792386282Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}